{"unit_id": "trace_0001", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 2, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 18, "function_name": "main"}, "text": "Last lecture: overview of RL from verifiable rewards (policy gradient)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0002", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 3, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 19, "function_name": "main"}, "text": "This lecture: deep dive into the mechanics of policy gradient (e.g., GRPO)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0003", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 6, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 37, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**State** s: prompt + generated response so far", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0004", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 7, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 38, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Action** a: generate next token", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0005", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 8, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 40, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Rewards** R: how good the response is; we'll focus on:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0006", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 9, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 41, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "- Outcome rewards, which depend on the entire response", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0007", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 10, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 42, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "- Verifiable rewards, whose computation is deterministic", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0008", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 11, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 43, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "- Notions of discounting and bootstrapping are less applicable", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0009", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 12, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 44, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "Example: \"... Therefore, the answer is 3 miles.\"", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0010", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 13, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 46, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Transition probabilities** T(s' | s, a): deterministic s' = s + a", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0011", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 14, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 47, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "- Can do planning / test-time compute (unlike in robotics)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0012", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 15, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 48, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "- States are really made up (different from robotics), so a lot of flexibility", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0013", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 16, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 50, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Policy** π(a | s): just a language model (fine-tuned)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0014", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 17, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 52, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Rollout/episode/trajectory**: s → a → ... → a → a → R", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0015", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 18, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 53, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "**Objective**: maximize expected reward E[R]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0016", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 19, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 54, "function_name": "rl_setup_for_language_models"}, "text": "(where the expectation is taken over prompts s and response tokens a)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0017", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 23, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 58, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "For notational simplicity, let *a* denote the entire response.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0018", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 24, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 60, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "We want to maximize expected reward with respect to the policy π:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0019", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 25, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 61, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "E[R] = ∫ p(s) π(a | s) R(s, a)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0020", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 26, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 63, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Obvious thing to do is to take the gradient:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0021", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 27, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 64, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "∇ E[R] = ∫ p(s) ∇ π(a | s) R(s, a)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0022", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 28, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 65, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "∇ E[R] = ∫ p(s) π(a | s) ∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0023", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 29, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 66, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "∇ E[R] = E[∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a)]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0024", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 30, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 68, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Naive policy gradient:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0025", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 31, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 69, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Sample prompt s, sample response a ~ π(a | s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0026", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 32, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 70, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Update parameters based on ∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a) (same as SFT, but weighted by R(s, a))", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0027", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 33, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 72, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Setting: R(s, a) ∈ {0, 1} = whether response is correct or not", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0028", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 34, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 73, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Naive policy gradient only updates on correct responses", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0029", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 35, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 74, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Like SFT, but dataset changing over time as policy changes", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0030", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 36, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 76, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Challenge: high noise/variance", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0031", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 37, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 77, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "In this setting, sparse rewards (few responses get reward 1, most get 0)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0032", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 38, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 78, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "In contrast: in RLHF, reward models (learned from pairwise preferences) are more continuous", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0033", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 39, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 80, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "### Baselines", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0034", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 40, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 81, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Recall ∇ E[R] = E[∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a)]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0035", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 41, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 82, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a) is an unbiased estimate of ∇ E[R], but maybe there are others with lower variance...", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0036", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 42, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 84, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Example: two states", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0037", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 43, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 85, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- s1: a1 → reward 11, a2 → reward 9", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0038", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 44, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 86, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- s2: a1 → reward 0, a2 → reward 2", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0039", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 45, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 87, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Don't want s1 → a2 (reward 9) because a1 is better, want s2 → a2 (reward 2), but 9 > 2", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0040", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 46, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 89, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Idea: maximize the baselined reward: E[R - b(s)]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0041", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 47, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 90, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "This is just E[R] shifted by a constant E[b(s)] that doesn't depend on the policy π", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0042", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 48, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 91, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "We update based on ∇ log π(a | s) (R(s, a) - b(s))", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0043", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 49, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 93, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "What b(s) should we use?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0044", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 50, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 95, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Example: two states", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0045", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 51, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 96, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Assuming uniform distribution over (s, a) and |∇ π(a | s)| = 1", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0046", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 53, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 98, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Define baseline b(s1) = 10, b(s2) = 1", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0047", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 55, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 100, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Variance reduced from 5.323 to 1.155", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0048", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 56, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 102, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Optimal b*(s) = E[(∇ π(a | s))^2 R | s] / E[(∇ π(a | s))^2 | s] (for one-parameter models)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0049", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 57, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 103, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "This is difficult to compute...", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0050", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 58, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 104, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "...so heuristic is to use the mean reward:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0051", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 59, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 105, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "b(s) = E[R | s]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0052", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 60, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 106, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "This is still hard to compute and must be estimated.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0053", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 61, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 108, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "### Advantage functions", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0054", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 62, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 109, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "This choice of b(s) has connections to advantage functions.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0055", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 63, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 110, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- V(s) = E[R | s] = expected reward from state s", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0056", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 64, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 111, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Q(s, a) = E[R | s, a] = expected reward from state s taking action a", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0057", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 65, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 112, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "(Note: Q and R are the same here, because we're assuming *a* has all actions and we have outcome rewards.)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0058", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 66, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 114, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Definition (advantage): A(s, a) = Q(s, a) - V(s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0059", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 67, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 115, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "Intuition: how much better is action a than expected from state s", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0060", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 68, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 117, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "If b(s) = E[R | s], then the baselined reward is identical to the advantage!", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0061", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 69, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 118, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "E[R - b(s)] = A(s, a)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0062", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 70, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 120, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "In general:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0063", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 71, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 121, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Ideal: E[∇ log π(a | s) R(s, a)]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0064", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 72, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 122, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "- Estimate: ∇ log π(a | s) δ", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0065", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 73, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 123, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "There are multiple choices of δ, as we'll see later.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0066", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 74, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 125, "function_name": "policy_gradient"}, "text": "[CS224R lecture notes]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0067", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 78, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 129, "function_name": "training_walkthrough"}, "text": "Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0068", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 78, "rendering_index": 2, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 129, "function_name": "training_walkthrough"}, "text": "DeepSeekMath: Pushing the Limits of Mathematical Reasoning in Open Language Models", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0069", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 79, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 130, "function_name": "training_walkthrough"}, "text": "- Simplification to PPO that removes the critic (value function)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0070", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 80, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 131, "function_name": "training_walkthrough"}, "text": "- Leverages the group structure in the LM setting (multiple responses per prompt), which provides a natural baseline b(s).", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0071", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 81, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 132, "function_name": "training_walkthrough"}, "text": "", "asset_path": "../../materials/spring2025-lectures/images/grpo-algorithm.png", "required": false}
