{"unit_id": "trace_0078", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 115, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 164, "function_name": "simple_task"}, "text": "Note that the second reward function provides more credit to the 3rd response than the first reward function.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0079", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 119, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 168, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Define a simple model that maps prompts to responses", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0080", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 120, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 169, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Assume fixed prompt and response length", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0081", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 121, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 170, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Captures positional information with separate per-position parameters", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0082", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 122, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 171, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Decode each position in the response independently (not autoregressive)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0083", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 131, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 175, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Start with a prompt s", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0084", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 133, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 178, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Generate responses a", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0085", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 151, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 182, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Compute rewards R of these responses:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0086", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 221, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 185, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Compute deltas δ given the rewards R (for performing the updates)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0087", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 256, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 191, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Compute log probabilities of these responses:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0088", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 273, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 194, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Compute loss so that we can use to update the model parameters", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0089", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 281, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 219, "function_name": "freezing_parameters"}, "text": "Motivation: in GRPO you'll see ratios: p(a | s) / p_old(a | s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0090", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 282, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 220, "function_name": "freezing_parameters"}, "text": "When you're optimizing, it is important to freeze and not differentiate through p_old", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0091", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 289, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 228, "function_name": "freezing_parameters"}, "text": "Do it properly:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0092", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 320, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 204, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Sometimes, we can use an explicit KL penalty to regularize the model.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0093", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 321, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 205, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "This can be useful if you want RL a new capability into a model, but you don't want it to forget its original capabilities.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0094", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 322, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 206, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "KL(p || q) = E_{x ~ p}[log(p(x)/q(x))]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0095", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 323, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 207, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "KL(p || q) = E_{x ~ p}[-log(q(x)/p(x))]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0096", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 324, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 208, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "KL(p || q) = E_{x ~ p}[q(x)/p(x) - log(q(x)/p(x)) - 1] because E_{x ~ p}[q(x)/p(x)] = 1", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0097", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 329, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 211, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "Summary:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0098", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 330, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 212, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Generate responses", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0099", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 331, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 213, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Compute rewards R and δ (rewards, centered rewards, normalized rewards, max rewards)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0100", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 332, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 214, "function_name": "simple_model"}, "text": "- Compute log probs of responses", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
