{"unit_id": "trace_0109", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1027, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 547, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "This seems to help, as:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0110", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1028, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 548, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "- Suboptimal rewards get a negative gradient update, and", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0111", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1029, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 549, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "- If all the responses for a given prompt have the same reward, then we don't update.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0112", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1030, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 550, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "Overall, this is better, but we're still getting stuck in local optima.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0113", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1031, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 552, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "Finally, let's try normalizing by the standard deviation.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0114", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1033, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 554, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "", "asset_path": "var/policy_gradient_normalized_rewards_naive.png", "required": false}
{"unit_id": "trace_0115", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1034, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 555, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "There is not much difference here, and indeed, variants like Dr. GRPO do not perform this normalization to avoid length bias (not an issue here since all responses have the same length.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0116", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1034, "rendering_index": 2, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 555, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "Understanding R1-Zero-Like Training: A Critical Perspective", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "trace_0117", "source_type": "official_trace_block", "source_id": "official_trace", "loc": {"trace_step": 1035, "rendering_index": 1, "path": "lecture_17.py", "line_number": 557, "function_name": "experiments"}, "text": "Overall, as you can see, reinforcement learning is not trivial, and you can easily get stuck in suboptimal states.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
